1. A flexible lighting element comprising:  

a flexible substrate;  

a plurality of conductive traces disposed on or in the flexible substrate;  

at least one flip-chip light emitting diode electrically coupled to the plurality of conductive traces, the flip-chip light emitting diode having a light-emitting surface oriented to emit light away from the flexible substrate;  

a transparent layer disposed over the at least one flip-chip light emitting diode such that light emitted by the flip-chip light emitting diode passes through the transparent layer; and  

one or more conductors electrically coupled to the flip-chip light emitting diode and positioned in an optical path associated with the transparent layer,  

wherein the one or more conductors comprise transparent conductive material, conductors hidden from view, or a combination thereof, and  

wherein a region of the flexible lighting element including the transparent layer and the one or more conductors has a visible light transmittance of at least 70%.

A flexible lighting assembly comprising:

a first substrate that is flexible and at least partially transparent;

a first conductive element disposed on the first substrate;

a second conductive element disposed on the first substrate and spaced apart from the first conductive element;

a light-emitting element electrically coupled to the first conductive element and the second conductive element, the light-emitting element being configured to emit light upon application of electrical power through the first and second conductive elements;

a first transparent layer disposed over at least a portion of the first conductive element, the second conductive element, and the light-emitting element; and

a second transparent layer disposed on an opposite side of the first substrate from the first transparent layer or over the first transparent layer,

wherein the first conductive element and the second conductive element are configured such that, when the flexible lighting assembly is viewed from a viewing side, the first conductive element and the second conductive element are not readily visible to an unaided human eye, and

wherein at least a portion of the flexible lighting assembly including the first substrate, the first transparent layer, and the second transparent layer has a visible-light transmittance of at least 70%.

1. A flexible lighting device comprising:

a flexible substrate that is substantially transparent to visible light;

a transparent layer spaced from the flexible substrate, the transparent layer being substantially transparent to visible light;

a transparent affixing layer disposed between and bonding the flexible substrate to the transparent layer;

at least one light-emitting diode disposed between the flexible substrate and the transparent layer, the at least one light-emitting diode having a first electrical contact and a second electrical contact located on a same surface of the at least one light-emitting diode; and

a plurality of conductors carried by the flexible substrate, the plurality of conductors including a first conductor electrically connected to the first electrical contact and a second conductor electrically connected to the second electrical contact,

wherein the flexible lighting device is bendable and, in regions outside the at least one light-emitting diode and the plurality of conductors, remains substantially transparent to visible light.
